  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 showed scVI (n200) improves RNA-only accuracy from 0.485 (PCA) to 0.520, and config_016 showed adding ResNet50 image with concat fusion to PCA RNA yields 0.527. However, we have no evidence on whether the scVI encoder gain is additive with the multimodal gain or whether it interacts with the image modality. Question: config_028 (multimodal, single profile, scVI n200, ResNet50, concat) is a single-variable change from config_016 (PCA→scVI), directly testing whether the learned-encoder improvement transfers to the multimodal setting. If it exceeds 0.527, the encoder and modality gains are independent and we should build on scVI going forward; if it plateaus near 0.520, the image contribution was specific to PCA's high-dimensional features; if it drops below 0.527, scVI's lower dimensionality may be incompatible with the current fusion. This is the highest-information next step because it resolves the most consequential open question—whether to anchor future multiprofile/fusion experiments on scVI or PCA—while changing only one variable relative to the current best configuration."
}

